window.docContents[74].resolve({"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes--How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family--The-rendered-definitions":{"contents":"Every @[pkc_math] application in the worked examples, with the clauses each requested.\n\n* Definition* Rendering mode* What it is* attenuationQ* plain* The vegetation attenuation τ = exp(−2·b·ndvi), kind attenuationK.* lavsForwardQ* substituting (1 step(s))* The LAVS forward σ⁰ = a·ndvi + (τ·c)·r + d, kind backscatter.* lavsJacResidualQ* substituting (1 step(s))* The four analytic Jacobian columns ∂residual/∂(a,b,c,d), each at its forced kind.* lavsResidualQ* substituting (2 step(s))* The LAVS residual s0 − σ⁰, kind backscatter (subtraction forces the shared kind).* avsForward* plain* The AVS-style backscatter forward model, rendered on its doc page as σ⁰ = a·ndvi + exp(−2·b·ndvi)·c·r + d.* byPolarization* plain* Case analysis on the polarization, written vertical-first.* columns* plain* Three columns returned as a triple: exercises the Prod.mk flattening and both head layouts.* combined* plain* Consumes a destructured pair.* model* substituting (1 step(s))* One derivation step.* noted* plain* Base backscatter.* residual* substituting (2 step(s))* The residual of model: two cumulative steps, so the reader sees the call, then the call expanded, then the constant it bottoms out in.* scaled* plain* Reads a configuration constant.* scaledByTwo* plain* Doubling through the numeral injection.* shared* keeping* A model with a shared intermediate: d is used by both s and the sum.* spread* plain* A record-valued model: renders as the system hi = a·b, lo = a − b.* twiceBound* keeping* A definition that binds u twice, for different values.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009How a definition reads — the rendering family","header":"31.8.5. The rendered definitions","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes--How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family--The-rendered-definitions"}});